Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain: a chain of edges whose curves cannot be
concatenated stays as its edges. Merging a chain concatenates the edges'
p-curves on the faces that are not planes (UnionPCurves, with
Geom2dConvert::ConcatC1) after a chain of lines or circles, and their 3D
curves (GlueEdgesWith3DCurves, with GeomConvert::ConcatC1) for a chain of
B-splines. Both throw ("Courbes non jointives") where the end of one curve
lies farther from the start of the next than the tolerance of the vertex
between them. The exception left the whole unification (the face merge
after a boolean, BRepAlgoAPI_BuilderAlgo::SimplifyResult) unfinished, so a
join or cut whose result was valid failed. MergeSubSeq now returns false
for such a chain, as it does for chains it cannot merge otherwise: their
edges are kept, and the rest of the shape is unified as before. (In the safe
input mode the chain's end vertices may already have been replaced by
copies of themselves, as for a chain that merges: the same points and
tolerances.)

Failures (mitcad#1986): the handlers catch only the concatenations' own
reports that two curves of the chain do not join: Geom2dConvert's (a
Standard_Failure thrown as such, "Courbes non jointives", from its
continuity check) for the p-curves, and GeomConvert's for the 3D curves
(GeomLProp's continuity check throws the same Standard_Failure as such,
ConcatC1 a Standard_ConstructionError for curves not C0). MergeSubSeq reports that
failure as it reports a chain it cannot merge (false), so the chain stays
as its edges; any other failure is rethrown and the unification fails as
before.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 0110.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
index 49f685922..635f191a8 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 #include <ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.hxx>
 
 #include <BRep_Builder.hxx>
+#include <Standard_ConstructionError.hxx>
+#include <typeinfo>
 #include <BRep_Tool.hxx>
 #include <BRepLib.hxx>
 #include <BRepTopAdaptor_TopolTool.hxx>
@@ -2386,7 +2388,23 @@ bool ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain::MergeSubSeq(
     B.Add(E, V[1]);
     B.UpdateVertex(V[0], 0., E, 0.);
     B.UpdateVertex(V[1], dist, E, 0.);
-    UnionPCurves(theChain, E);
+    // A chain whose p-curves cannot be concatenated (their ends farther
+    // apart than the tolerance of the vertex between them) stays as its
+    // edges, instead of failing the whole unification.
+    try
+    {
+      UnionPCurves(theChain, E);
+    }
+    catch (Standard_Failure const& anException)
+    {
+      // (Geom2dConvert's report that two p-curves do not join, thrown as a
+      // Standard_Failure as such; any other failure is rethrown.)
+      if (typeid(anException) != typeid(Standard_Failure))
+      {
+        throw;
+      }
+      return false;
+    }
     OutEdge = E;
     return true;
   }
@@ -2513,7 +2531,20 @@ bool ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain::MergeSubSeq(
       B.UpdateVertex(V[0], 0., E, 0.);
       B.UpdateVertex(V[1], lpar, E, 0.);
     }
-    UnionPCurves(theChain, E);
+    try
+    {
+      UnionPCurves(theChain, E);
+    }
+    catch (Standard_Failure const& anException)
+    {
+      // (Geom2dConvert's report that two p-curves do not join, thrown as a
+      // Standard_Failure as such; any other failure is rethrown.)
+      if (typeid(anException) != typeid(Standard_Failure))
+      {
+        throw;
+      }
+      return false;
+    }
     OutEdge = E;
     return true;
   }
@@ -2550,7 +2581,27 @@ bool ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain::MergeSubSeq(
     }
     if (NeedUnion)
     {
-      OutEdge = GlueEdgesWith3DCurves(theChain, VF, VL);
+      // A chain whose curves cannot be concatenated (their ends farther
+      // apart than the tolerance of the vertex between them) stays as its
+      // edges, as chains of other curves that cannot be merged do, instead
+      // of failing the whole unification.
+      try
+      {
+        OutEdge = GlueEdgesWith3DCurves(theChain, VF, VL);
+      }
+      catch (Standard_Failure const& anException)
+      {
+        // (GeomConvert's reports that two curves do not join: GeomLProp's
+        // continuity check throws a Standard_Failure as such, ConcatC1 a
+        // Standard_ConstructionError for curves not C0; any other failure
+        // is rethrown.)
+        if (typeid(anException) != typeid(Standard_Failure)
+            && dynamic_cast<const Standard_ConstructionError*>(&anException) == nullptr)
+        {
+          throw;
+        }
+        return false;
+      }
       return true;
     }
   }
